 "notes": "ADMX Run1B (data taken Jan-Oct 2018). 90% CL exclusion on g_agamma vs axion mass from Fig.4 (raster PNG run1b_sensitivity_prelim.png; no ancillary data). Headline curve = 'This work' green forest; I traced the darker-green Maxwell-Boltzmann (MB) standard-halo fill (rho_a=0.45 GeV/cm^3, per Eq.1 and Ref.[30]). The lighter-green companion is the N-body-halo result (rho_a=0.63 GeV/cm^3, Ref.[31]) which reaches slightly lower; not reported here. Curve is per-column bottom edge of the excluded fill, binned (median) to ~60 points. Two gaps preserved: ~726.6 MHz and the wide ~747-760 MHz (753.844 MHz) mode-crossing regions where no limit set (Table I); three narrower mode crossings (704.7,715.1,717.0 MHz) are sub-pixel and not resolved. Axes calibrated from tick marks: freq 625-825 MHz (x), g_agamma 1e-16 to 1e-14 log (y); mass=4.135667e-9*f[MHz] eV; y-cal cross-checked against KSVZ(~1.2e-15) and DFSZ(~4.6e-16) black reference lines. Limit excludes DFSZ over 2.81-3.31 ueV. Edge points near 3.31 ueV rise as sensitivity falls off.",
